Obviously, there is no extra mask argument at present. However, I wonder if you can simply write a distance function that uses a named fine mask in the current workspace? Remembering that the distance matrix output needs to be in terms of the coarse mask (from each detector to each coarse-mask point). This would be ad hoc and not easy to generalise or package, if that's your goal.
Murray

