1) Yes, just specify the appropriate argument from nlm or optim. It will get passed along to the maximizing function via the ... ('dots') argument of secr.fit
2) Not sure what is going on here. Your newdata implies all S1 are visibility 0 and all S2 are visibility 1; to get all combinations you could use expand.grid() instead of data.frame(), but I doubt that is the issue. Your second example fails because session must be a factor with (I assume) the levels S1 and S2. Hence session = factor("S1", levels = c("S1","S2")) is more likely to work, but will probably bring you back to the other issue, whatever that is.

